implementationPlan.description:
VERIFY ONCE, fresh, from the repo root on WSL:

node --test scripts/tests/protected-agent-command.test.mjs && bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh

It must exit 0. Its command, exit code and output tail are complete_task's evidence; say whether the pwsh rows ran or were skipped. Also run `bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh`, `pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/tests/parity-check.ps1` when pwsh exists, and the existing R13c2 marker rows (postflight.sh's P rows), and report them, so the shared marker block is not regressed.

Mutants, on scratch copies, each turning the named rows red:
(i) a prefix match (claude*): R1;
(ii) `command -v` instead of the manual scan: T1 or T2;
(iii) no in-project skip: T3;
(iv) the gate placed after the MCP config write: R1's no-config assertion;
(v) the gate active without the marker: L1.

A read-only `git status --short` must show only the three owned paths. moe-agent.sh/.ps1 are hot files: if a peer row has unlanded hunks in them, never sweep, revert or stash them. Coordinate in chat instead.
